flowchart TB
  %% QUESTION THIS DIAGRAM ANSWERS: after the supplier is paid, the budget records stop. In which records does the purchased item continue, and who is responsible for it?
  %% READING: read from top to bottom. A solid arrow leads to the next stage. The dotted arrow with the label "next year" shows that use and count are repeated each year. The other dotted arrow shows a report that is made in addition to the main sequence. Blue = property, plant and equipment.
  %% IDEA: the budget follows money for one year. An asset lives for many years. It is followed in property records (who holds the item) and in accounting records (what it is worth). The two must agree with a physical count each year.
  %% SOURCES: capitalization threshold of PHP 50,000, semi-expendable property (low-valued up to PHP 5,000, high-valued above that), Inventory Custodian Slip, annual Report on the Physical Count of Property, Plant and Equipment as of 31 December [COA2022-004]. Property, plant and equipment register in BTMS, asset transactions create journal entries [CL2025-8][BTMS-SITE]. National Asset Registry System of BTr, agency asset management plans [BTR-SYS][ROADMAP2024]. Monitoring of non-financial assets through the national registry is not yet in full use and does not record the age of assets (indicator 12.2, score C), rules on disposal rated B (indicator 12.3) [PEFA2025]. Procurement plan [RA12009 s.7]. Bonding of accountable officers by BTr [EO449].
  %% GENERAL KNOWLEDGE, NOT OPENED IN A SOURCE HERE: inspection and acceptance report, Property Acknowledgment Receipt, property card and ledger card, depreciation, insurance with GSIS, the report of unserviceable property, the disposal committee and the modes of disposal. Check Government Accounting Manual Volume I (chapter on property, plant and equipment) and Volume II (forms).

  A["1  PLAN<br/>need stated in the procurement plan<br/>and in the agency asset management plan"]
  B["2  ACQUIRE<br/>procurement and contract (chapter 06).<br/>Other ways: construction, donation, transfer"]
  C["3  RECEIVE<br/>delivery inspected and accepted.<br/>Record: inspection and acceptance report"]
  Q{"Unit cost<br/>PHP 50,000<br/>or more?"}
  D1["4a  PROPERTY, PLANT AND EQUIPMENT<br/>recorded as an asset and depreciated over its useful life.<br/>Records: PPE ledger card (accounting unit),<br/>property card (property unit), PPE register in BTMS"]:::ppe
  D2["4b  SEMI-EXPENDABLE PROPERTY<br/>below PHP 50,000. Expensed when issued, but still tracked.<br/>Low-valued: up to PHP 5,000. High-valued: above PHP 5,000"]
  E1["5a  ISSUE TO THE USER<br/>Property Acknowledgment Receipt:<br/>a named officer accepts responsibility"]:::ppe
  E2["5b  ISSUE TO THE USER<br/>Inventory Custodian Slip:<br/>a named officer accepts responsibility"]
  F["6  USE<br/>maintenance, insurance, transfer between<br/>units or agencies (each transfer is recorded)"]
  G["7  COUNT<br/>physical count each year as of 31 December.<br/>Record: Report on the Physical Count of PPE.<br/>Differences with the books are investigated"]
  H["8  NATIONAL REGISTER<br/>strategically important assets (land, buildings,<br/>roads, dams) reported to the National<br/>Asset Registry System of BTr"]
  I["9  DISPOSE<br/>unserviceable items inspected, appraised and<br/>disposed by a committee: sale, transfer or destruction.<br/>Proceeds go to the Treasury"]
  J["10  REMOVE FROM THE BOOKS<br/>journal entry, property records closed"]

  A --> B --> C --> Q
  Q -- "yes" --> D1 --> E1 --> F
  Q -- "no" --> D2 --> E2 --> F
  F --> G --> I --> J
  G -.-> H
  G -. "next year" .-> F

  W["REPORTED WEAKNESS (PEFA 2025, indicator 12.2, score C): the monitoring of non-financial assets through<br/>the national registry is not yet in full use, and the registry does not record the age of assets.<br/>The budget records and the asset records are linked by documents, not by a common code:<br/>the contract number and the property number are different identifiers (see 17d)."]
  J ~~~ W

